    "text": "The WorldLines paper explicitly frames memory-to-plan translation as a technique for rebuilding world states under partial observability and overwritten memory, not as an independent fundamental challenge.",
    "topic": "framing in WorldLines"
  },
  {
    "text": "The fundamental challenges WorldLines addresses are partial observability and memory overwriting; translating long-term memory into plans is the proposed solution, not the problem itself.",
    "topic": "problem-solution relationship"
  },
  {
    "text": "In the WorldLines architecture, memory-to-plan translation is instrumental for inferring unobserved state from episodic memory, making it a means to an end rather than an end in itself.",
    "topic": "architectural role"
  }
